 About, Copyright Notice.
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

                                AMFETAMiN v2.0,

                  Last Callers Util for AmiExpress BBS Clones
                Written by The Silencer / doodles^shock in 1994

                         Copyright ©1994 The Silencer
                  Permission is granted to freely distribute
                this product for non-commercial purposes only,
                    as long as all files remain unmodified.

     AMFETAMiN is written in highly optimized C code for best performance!

·Why Did I Make a Last Caller Util ?

 Well, to be honest I decided to make one when I saw a local BBS that had
 Macromans PowerCaller installed that looked like shit and was written in
 ARexx. BTW He ripped the fucking code from a dude in the US that a friend
 of mine multichatted with on sum US board, he was quite pissed at macroman
 for this! Don't remember the dudes name but I guess macroman do.

 Shortly after this release there will be another one with sum updates.
 Ascii output aswell, stripped code, more configurable etc..












 Features:
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
· Quick As A Flash,
  Totally Independent of Callerslog FileSize! Scans a 5Mb Callerslog
  as fast as a 1kb Callerslog.
  The Only Thing Slowing It Down Is Harddrive Fragmentation :)

· Supports More Than 10 Nodes (0-9) Since New /X Can Handle Up To 32 Nodes.
  Amfetamin Can Handle Up To 99 Nodes So There Will Be No Conflict With
  Future /X Upgrades.

· Supports All Baudrates From 0(?) Up To 100.000 Baud (21.600, 28.800+ Etc.)
  No Conflict With New(Higher/Lower?) Baudrates/Modemtypes.

· Supports CPS Rates Over 10.000 (21.600+ TextFileTransfers? Etc.)
  Up To 99.999 CPS Can Be Recorded.

· Byte Values Shown In Kilobytes Or Megabytes Depending On The Filesizes.

· No Temporary DataFiles Or So Needed, It Uses It's Own Output As Datafile.

· Doesn't Crash & Burn, if it failures it exits safe with the apropriate
  errormessage.

· Are Able To Display As Many LastCallers As You Like, Say 100.000 ?

· GREAT LOOKS!













 Installation:
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 AMFETAMiN.000 is the version optimized for 68000+ systems
 AMFETAMiN.030 is optimized for 68020+ systems

 Just Add this To Your Logoff-Script:

 AMFETAMiN.xxx <output> <node> <calls> <sysop/nosysop>

        <output> Is The Textfile That Is Generated... Try RAM:Test.TXT
          <node> The Node To Process
         <calls> How Many Calls That Should Be Shown (Unlimited Amount!)
 <sysop/nosysop> If Local_Sysop Logins Should Be Recorded

 All <arguments> Are Ofcuz cASEiNSENSiTiVe.


 Ex.
 ~~~
 AMFETAMiN BBS:Bull.TXT 1 12 NoSysop

 This Line Generates a Last Callers List For Node 1 Displaying Only The
 12 Last Callers. Local Sysop Logins Will Not Show!













